ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":116,"prev":118,"next":121,"titles":124,"firmware":47},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":11,"order":12,"path":13,"context":14,"summary":17,"status":18,"firmware":19,"facts":25,"procedures":79,"parameters":95,"related":96,"body":101,"sources":102,"official_url":29,"controls":113},"com.mtp","MTP mode (file transfer)",[5,6,7,8,9,10],"mtp","media transfer protocol","file transfer","usb drive","field kit","eject","com",60,"knowledge/manual/units/com/mtp.md",{"modes":15,"screens":16},[],[5],"`com → M4` lets a connected computer browse the OP-XY's storage and copy projects, samples and presets; `M4` ejects. Macs need TE's field kit app, and USB MIDI is off while MTP runs.","current",{"min":20,"changed_in":21,"guide_version":23,"verified_on":24},"1.0.9",[22,23],"1.0.32","1.1.15",null,[26,31,34,38,40,43,49,52,55,59,62,65,68,71,75],{"id":27,"text":28,"source":29,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"enter","`com → M4` switches on MTP, so a computer can read and write the projects, samples and presets on the unit.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/com#mtp","official",{"id":32,"text":33,"source":29,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"needs-computer","MTP is only offered while a computer is connected by USB, so plug in first.",{"id":35,"text":36,"source":37,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"mac","macOS cannot open MTP devices by itself, so Macs need TE's field kit app; Windows and Linux need nothing extra.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/fieldkit",{"id":10,"text":39,"source":29,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"`M4` on the MTP screen ejects the OP-XY from the computer.",{"id":41,"text":42,"source":37,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"m4-not-t4","Instructions that say `T4` for MTP (TE's sound-pack page among them) follow the OP-1 field; on the OP-XY it is `M4`.",{"id":44,"text":45,"source":46,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":47,"confidence":48},"midi-gone","In MTP mode the OP-XY shows up as a different USB device and its MIDI port disappears, so MIDI apps, this one included, lose the connection.","docs/research/90-device-probe.md#2026-09-26--session-1-results-owner-present-scratch-project-os-1133","1.1.33","verified",{"id":50,"text":51,"source":46,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":47,"confidence":48},"auto-exit","When the computer closes its MTP session, the OP-XY leaves MTP mode by itself and its MIDI port returns.",{"id":53,"text":54,"source":46,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":47,"confidence":48},"layout","On OS 1.1.33 the top level holds projects (user, templates and the open project as workspace.xy), samples (user), presets (snapshot and user sound packs) and how_to_import.txt.",{"id":56,"text":57,"source":58,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":47,"confidence":48},"own-folders","Each kind of file goes only in its own top folder (presets, projects, samples), and new folders can be made only inside those three; a copy that fails usually has a name the unit refuses or sits in the wrong folder.","docs/research/30-presets-samples.md#41-what-mtp-shows",{"id":60,"text":61,"source":58,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":47,"confidence":48},"preset-files","A copied drum or sampler preset is a folder whose name ends in .preset, its patch.json beside its samples; it can sit anywhere inside the presets folder, a folder of your own there included. A synth preset without samples can also be a single .json file.",{"id":63,"text":64,"source":58,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":47,"confidence":48},"on-eject","What you copy, rename or delete shows on the unit once the disk is ejected (`M4`).",{"id":66,"text":67,"source":58,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":47,"confidence":48},"names","The unit's own import note allows letters, digits, spaces, hashes, hyphens and round brackets in file and folder names, plus the extension's dot; keep to those even though OS 1.1.15 took UTF-8.",{"id":69,"text":70,"source":58,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":47,"confidence":48},"samples-travel","A project file does not carry its samples, so a project moved to another OP-XY needs its samples copied too.",{"id":72,"text":73,"source":74,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"bug-1029","OS 1.0.29 could corrupt files over 64 KB copied off the unit by MTP; 1.0.32 fixed it, and backups made under 1.0.29 may be damaged.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.0.32",{"id":76,"text":77,"source":78,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"utf8","MTP accepts UTF-8 file and folder names since OS 1.1.15.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.15",[80,89],{"id":27,"goal":81,"preconditions":82,"steps":85,"result":88,"source":29,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"Put the OP-XY in MTP mode",[83,84],"a computer is connected by USB-C","field kit runs on a Mac",[86],{"keys":87,"note":24,"set":24},"com → M4","The storage appears on the computer (inside field kit on a Mac).",{"id":10,"goal":90,"preconditions":91,"steps":92,"result":24,"source":29,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"Eject the OP-XY from the computer",[],[93],{"keys":94,"note":24,"set":24},"M4",[],[97,98,99,100],"howto.back-up-projects","howto.load-samples","com.usb","sampler.sample-files","MTP is a mode, not a background service: live MIDI and file transfer take turns. Eject with `M4`,\nor let the computer close the session, before unplugging.",[103,105,107,109,110,112],{"url":29,"kind":104},"guide",{"url":37,"kind":106},"te",{"url":46,"kind":108},"research",{"url":58,"kind":108},{"url":74,"kind":111},"changelog",{"url":78,"kind":111},[114,115],"key.com","key.m4",{"id":11,"title":117},"Connectivity",{"id":119,"title":120},"com.bluetooth-midi","Bluetooth MIDI",{"id":122,"title":123},"com.midi-cc-reference","MIDI CC reference",{"basics.key-notation":125,"basics.main-modes":126,"basics.modules":127,"basics.track-buttons":128,"basics.linked-tracks":129,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":130,"ba